Miracast: turn the screen-cast picture (ND_VIDEO_FLIP).

On wlroots compositors that turn a screen in software (a phone in
landscape), the screen-cast portal hands over the buffer as stored,
portrait, with the turn apart as metadata, which Network Displays
ignores: the TV showed the picture sideways and squeezed.  ND_VIDEO_FLIP
names a videoflip method (counterclockwise, clockwise,
rotate-180) to put after the portal's source; the caller knows the
screen's turn.  For fxtec-pro1x-guix (AGPL-3.0-or-later); the program's
own licence (GPL-3.0-or-later) applies to this change upstream.

--- a/src/app/nd-window.c	2026-11-22 00:57:08.316295826 +0100
+++ b/src/app/nd-window.c	2026-11-22 01:25:40.935417440 +0100
@@ -190,7 +190,25 @@
       gst_element_link_many (src, filter, dst, NULL);
     }
   else
-    gst_element_link_many (src, dst, NULL);
+    {
+      /* ND_VIDEO_FLIP: a videoflip method (counterclockwise...)
+       * for a screen the compositor turns in software, whose buffer the
+       * portal hands over as stored, its turn apart (wlroots on a phone:
+       * the picture came sideways and squeezed). */
+      const gchar *flip = g_getenv ("ND_VIDEO_FLIP");
+      GstElement *turn = NULL;
+
+      if (flip && *flip)
+        turn = gst_element_factory_make ("videoflip", "nd-video-flip");
+      if (turn)
+        {
+          gst_util_set_object_arg (G_OBJECT (turn), "method", flip);
+          gst_bin_add (bin, turn);
+          gst_element_link_many (src, turn, dst, NULL);
+        }
+      else
+        gst_element_link_many (src, dst, NULL);
+    }
 
   res = gst_element_factory_make ("intervideosrc", "screencastsrc");
   g_object_set (res,
